
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:fe_web@

%9Parameters:%9

    STATUS:     Displays whether the server is enabled, the number of
                connected clients and, for each client, its address, its
                server tag and the number of messages sent and received.

    Without any parameter, the status is displayed.

%9Description:%9

    Shows the status of fe-web, the WebSocket server that lets a web client
    (for example NexusIRC) show and use this erssi session from a browser.
    The fe_web module is loaded at startup by default (it is listed in the
    autoload_modules setting) when erssi is built with fe-web support.

    The server itself is controlled by the settings below. Changing any of
    them starts, stops or restarts the server, which disconnects the web
    clients; changing other settings does not touch it.

        fe_web_enabled (default: OFF)
            Runs the server.
        fe_web_port (default: 9001)
            The TCP port to listen on.
        fe_web_bind (default: 127.0.0.1)
            The address to listen on.
        fe_web_password (default: empty)
            The password a client must give. The server refuses to start
            while it is empty.

    Connections always use TLS (wss://) with a self-signed certificate that
    is generated when the server starts, and the messages are additionally
    encrypted with AES-256-GCM using a key derived from fe_web_password.

    Keep fe_web_bind on 127.0.0.1 and put the web client behind a TLS proxy
    or tunnel if it has to be reached from elsewhere.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET fe_web_password a-long-random-secret
    /SET fe_web_bind 127.0.0.1
    /SET fe_web_enabled ON
    /FE_WEB
    /FE_WEB STATUS

%9See also:%9 LOAD, SET

